## G. Release acceptance checklist for first replacement slice

Do not claim replacement until all mandatory items for the chosen workflow are evidenced:

- [ ] Owner selected first workflow, deployment profile, runtime strategy and explicit exclusions; decisions recorded in `decisions.md`.
- [ ] User workflow and incumbent baseline are reproducible with version/config/source recorded.
- [ ] Plaesy task/run/message identifiers and state transitions persist across restart.
- [ ] Agent principal is authenticated and authorized for the project/task/tools; revocation tested.
- [ ] Delivery states distinguish queued, runtime-accepted, acknowledged, failed and unknown; no false “seen” claim.
- [ ] Duplicate delivery, lost ack, timeout, crash, stale lease, offline recipient and retry are fault-tested.
- [ ] Tool permissions, budgets, cancellation and secret redaction are verified with synthetic inputs.
- [ ] Output artifact and actual test evidence are attached; completion cannot be inferred from agent prose alone.
- [ ] Concurrent work either uses isolated worktrees or has tested enforced write/conflict handling.
- [ ] Backup/export/import and rollback tested before any cutover; incumbent remains usable through parallel-run.
- [ ] Focused tests rerun on the integrated checkout; limitations, backend dependencies and residual risks documented.

## H. Agent work protocol (avoid repeating research)

1. Read this checklist plus [open decisions](decisions.md), [current-state assessment](current-state-assessment.md), and the feature’s linked spec before starting.
2. Search the cited implementation/test paths and prior comparison notes. If evidence is missing, update the existing row/note; do not start an unbounded vendor survey.
3. Take one row or disjoint set of rows as the task boundary. State files owned, acceptance criteria, and dependencies before parallel edits.
4. Report exact paths changed, commands and observed outcomes, evidence label, and remaining unknowns. Do not promote design-only to implemented.
5. Integrator reviews the combined diff and reruns focused tests. Update status only after that verification.

